# FieldReport — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
FieldReport is a mobile-first SaaS for trades contractors (roofers, inspectors, restoration, HVAC, fencing, property managers, and any other trade).
Contractors photograph a job site, narrate observations, and receive a professional branded report in minutes.

## Product mode
- Demo and live share the same API routes, store client, and UI flows.
- Demo mode (default): no cloud credentials; server persists to `.fieldreport/` via `DemoRepository`.
- Live mode: set Supabase + Stripe + Resend (+ OpenAI); `SupabaseRepository` and production services activate automatically.
- Never crash public pages when unconfigured.

## AI-first reports (non-negotiable)
- OpenAI is the **primary** report author when `OPENAI_API_KEY` is set: full structure, prose, recommendations, photo vision, PDF alignment, and **photo highlight overlays** (colored rectangles on findings).
- Taxonomy / rule engine is a **fail-safe fallback only** when OpenAI is unset or errors — never the preferred path. Fallback still attaches heuristic photo overlays from captions/notes.
- Customer reports **include job photos** with severity-colored annotation boxes matching section findings.
- Users may upload any reference PDF; extracted text is evidence and AI aligns report structure to it.
- Scanned PDFs: when plain-text extract is empty and OpenAI is configured, page images are OCR’d via vision before save.
- Voice/typed notes update findings (selected photo transcription or job notes) — they do not rewrite the PDF. Regenerating rebuilds/patches the report from all current evidence and is free (does not consume monthly credits).
- Reports keep version history (last 10) on regenerate; share URL stays on the current report id.
- Monthly report counters roll over automatically by UTC month key.
- Report scopes are freeform (any trade description). Catalog templates are optional shortcuts, not limits.
- Voice: Whisper transcription when OpenAI is configured; browser SpeechRecognition otherwise; typed notes always available. Tap a photo to choose the note target.
- Email: in-app compose + send (Resend when configured; demo logs otherwise). Contact Picker, paste/CSV import, recent + job-history emails; multi-recipient supported. Google/iCloud OAuth sync is out of MVP.
- Do not invent measurements the inspector did not provide (AI prompts and engine must enforce this).

## Tech stack
- Next.js App Router (TypeScript)
- Tailwind CSS
- Demo store on server; API client in browser
- Capacitor iOS/Android shell (`app.fieldreport.mobile`) loading the hosted app for store distribution
- Native parity: Capacitor Camera, Share, deep links, offline banner, safe areas, mic permission preflight
- RevenueCat for native IAP; Stripe for web checkout
- Real forgot/reset password (demo token + live Supabase email)
- Playwright for UI smoke tests; gap/live/native harness suites (see SMOKE-MATRIX.md)
- tsx scripts for report-engine, mocked AI path, PDF extract, naming, billing, contacts

## Monetization
- Free / Starter / Pro / Team report limits
- Web: Stripe Checkout (optional trial via STRIPE_TRIAL_DAYS)
- Native: RevenueCat + App Store / Play subscriptions; webhook + client sync update `profile.plan`
- Judge / promo unlock: `SHIPATON-JUDGE` → Pro (see SHIPATON.md)
- Credential / DB / route naming: see NAMING-CONVENTIONS.md (`npm run test:naming`)
- Launch runbook before/after credentials: LAUNCH.md (`npm run check:launch`)

## UX rules
- Mobile-first, sunlight-readable, 44px minimum touch targets
- Empty, loading, error, and success states on every async flow
- Voice notes AND typed field notes (never block on microphone)
- Reports must look professional enough to send to a customer or insurer
- Zero hard limits on which trades or report scopes users can describe

## Taxonomy (fallback / suggestions only)
- Catalog lives in `src/lib/taxonomy/` for onboarding suggestions and offline fallback sections.
- Onboarding preferences filter **shortcuts**, not allowed scopes.
- Universal templates: `general`, `move_in_out`. Legacy slugs remain valid via alias map.
- Rule engine reads section headings only when AI is unavailable.

## Business logic
- Free: 3 reports/month
- Starter: $29 — 30 reports/month
- Pro: $59 — unlimited
- Team: $99 — unlimited for this account (multi-seat invites are roadmap; not enforced as a separate org product in MVP)
- Native field capture uses Capacitor Camera on iOS/Android; web uses file input with capture
